  question: "Two authorities name the accelerators in this unit and answer DIFFERENTLY: the operator reported two Tesla T10 (2026-11-15 and 2026-11-17, and the same operator's own session named a third card -- 'third card: serial 1323019027149, in SLOT2 (c1:00.0)'), while the unit itself enumerates three driver-visible NVIDIA functions with three UUIDs and three serials. Which is the unit? The read rows carry THREE boards because a unit's enumeration outranks a report about it, and the report row still says TWO because a report row describes its report -- so the disagreement is visible on both sides instead of being resolved by deleting one. Closing it does NOT need the vendor:device read -- that was taken in the same session once the sysfs paths carried the PCI domain (every function read vendor 0x10de device 0x1e37, unit_read2.txt), and only the earlier unprefixed-path attempt failed. What it needs is the operator's word on the count: whether one of the two-report statements miscounted, or a fourth card exists that the driver does not show; and the ownership read of which machine answers on 192.168.1.236, which no read in this repo can yet repeat. Until then no consumer may treat this unit's GPU count as settled. THAT CLOSING CONDITION IS NOW MET, and the date of meeting is the operator's own read of 2026-11-19: the same three cards, 01:00.0 / 81:00.0 / c1:00.0, which is what the receipts had already enumerated. So the two-card statements are the stale side of the fork, THREE is this unit's count, and the row is Integrated at 218429cecebd204441ac8323b304687d4ae537e7. The 192.168.1.236 half of the sentence above is NOT settled by that -- no read in this repo can repeat it, and the enrollment row stays HostKeyLoginRefused; that question lives on in h11ssl_unit3_host_key_login_admits_on_no_read_the_fleet_can_repeat, and it was never this row's fork.",
